{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-single-project-tsx","path":"/projects/before-you-go-art-installation","result":{"data":{"project":{"Completed":"5 years ago","dateCompleted":"2021-09-01","Title":"Before You Go Art Installation","RepoLink":"https://github.com/NightingaleMedia/BeforeYouGo","LiveLink":"https://github.com/NightingaleMedia/BeforeYouGo","skills":[{"skill":{"Link":"https://www.raspberrypi.com/for-home/","Mastery":"Mastered","SkillName":"Raspberry Pi"},"SkillCategory":"creative"},{"skill":{"Link":"https://nodejs.org/en/about/","Mastery":"Mastered","SkillName":"Node.js"},"SkillCategory":"backend"}],"Narrative":{"data":{"childMarkdownRemark":{"html":"<p>Winner of the ArtPrize $50,000 grand prize!</p>\n<p>An idea that combines technology, storytelling, immersive experience and art in one.  I partnered with an artist/designer to help bring an idea to life.</p>\n<p>Before You Go is an art installation that made its winning debut at the Grand Rapids ArtPrize in 2021, a lauded and international art fair with thousands of entries.  To our great surprise and excitement, the installation won the first place prize in the whole event winning over $60,000 in prizes.  I was honored to be a part of such an innovative and unique installation.</p>\n<h4>Gathering the Source Files</h4>\n<p>The project involved gathering 400+ audio clips of interviews from people across the country.  Candidates could call a hotline to leave a message or record audio and send it in.  We also conducted hundreds of in-person interviews from candidates young and old.  The subjects were asked broad questions regarding their life, their story, their regrets, fears and hopes.  Every clip was placed into one of 9 categories that corresponded to</p>\n<h4>Hacking a Phone Booth</h4>\n<p>After assembling hundreds of short audio clips, we needed to make them all accesible in a user interface.  We found an old prison phone that still had a dial pad and handset intact.  I started by reading through the matrix language that operates grid dial pads and DTMF (dual tone multi-frequency) that controls standard phones.</p>\n<p>I measured the wires coming from the dial-pad and was able to sort them and place them into the inputs of a Raspberry Pi.  We then created a simple menu system using a state-machine and python from the pi.  The audio was routed out of the pi and we also hooked</p>\n<p>Our team built a 2021 version of a phone booth. Users can immersively interact with a real phone. The audio has been replaced with a cloud-based dataset of 400+ interviews and clips from around the country. Users can also record their own. Currently being expanded to web and VOIP services.</p>"}}},"tags":[{"tagName":"Creative Coding"},{"tagName":"sound design"}],"Cover":{"alternativeText":"b4yg.png","localFile":{"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/sigman-public-assets/b4yg_77ccc6925f/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png","childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fullWidth","backgroundColor":"#080808","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/7185b/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png","srcSet":"/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/f054e/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png 750w,\n/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/7185b/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png 754w","sizes":"100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/4f03f/b4yg_77ccc6925f.webp 750w,\n/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/4cdee/b4yg_77ccc6925f.webp 754w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"100vw"}]},"width":1,"height":1},"fixed":{"base64":"data:image/png;base64,","width":400,"height":400,"src":"/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/497c6/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png","srcSet":"/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/497c6/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png 1x,\n/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/2a4de/b4yg_77ccc6925f.png 1.5x"}}}},"Gallery":[{"localFile":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fullWidth","backgroundColor":"#080808","images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/dd10161d01c5dd5d5fd04b1dde852ef5/7185b/b4yg_57